After ascending by the first time, I decided to go out in a hunt for
the supposedly toughest opponent in the game-- Demogorgon.

Having heard the stories about the sheer nastiness of my opponent, I
carefully gathered a complete 'Fenrir's version of a Demogorgon Kit'
which was composed of:

- Some decent weapons (the +5 Excalibur and some silver saber which
was not even blessed)
- A not so decent weapon to whack Orcus with without killing him (I
used the blessed Magic Mirror of Merlin. Hahah!)
- A cursed, cheap plastic imitation of the AoY (for... um, good luck?)
- A ring of free action.
- Decent set of armor. (AC 27; including the usual ascension kit
stuff: boots of speed, cloak of mag res, gauntlets of power, SDSM,
etc)
- A /oW (0:2) (just in case, just in case...)
- A /oF (0:1) (had another one without charges, so when I got to the
'burn Elbereth on the upstairs part'... "You start writing in the dust
with a /oF" oops!)
- Some /oDigging
- And an uncursed unihorn instead of any other, reliable form.

And my skills were:

Two weapon - skilled
Long sword - skilled
Saber - unskilled (I had just found the thing lying on the ground,
serious!)

Once fully prepared, I descend into Gehennom, find Orcus, and start
bashing him with the Magic Mirror. Many hours later, I was about to
get convinced of that the fabled Demogorgon was nothing but a myth and
about to resume the exploration of Gehennom and ascend and all that --
but then, right when I wander off from the staircase, "Orcus casts a
spell! Monsters appear from nowhere! --more-- Demogorgon hits!
Demogorgon stings! You feel deathly sick! Demogorgon stings!
Demogorgon casts a spell!"

Eeek!

I beat Demogorgon up so he'll have to retreat to the up-staircase to
heal, and escape to the level below; there I use my uncursed unicorn
horn to cure the sickness and then return to the battle. I hit him, he
hits me, I hit him, he hits me, I go down to heal myself, then back,
and so on until I realize this wasn't getting anywhere; I wish for a
cursed potion of gain level and stand on the upstairs, burn the E-
word, hit him twice and then... WHAT?! He died already?

Either a) The RNG loves me and I have been stomach-churningly lucky,
or b) the Demogorgon of the current version is not really *THAT*
tough.

I'm going to try beating Demogorgon while trying for the illiterate
conduct next time...


